<title>INDIA: Indian Shipping -- Madras cargoes - Nov 29.</title>
<headline>Indian Shipping -- Madras cargoes - Nov 29.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is the berthing schedule of major vessels loading and unloading at India's Madras port on November 29:</p>
<p> Commodity		Tons		  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>		  (LDD/ULD)  (Balance)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Container	   182 (LDD)     90     Express Nilgiris 25/11</p>
<p> General	   5,317 (ULD)  1,113     Panglima	   24/11</p>
<p> General	     897 (LDD)  4,103     Panglima	   24/11</p>
<p> Steel	     1,978 (ULD)    ---     Prime - XI	 26/11</p>
<p> Granite Block   4,264 (LDD)    736     Haulin Express   25/11</p>
<p> Steel	     9,109 (ULD)  2,643     Belakun	    24/11</p>
<p> Met Coke	 13,348 (ULD)  8,652     China Mountain   26/11</p>
<p> Scrap	     5,490 (ULD) 26,010     World Themis     25/11</p>
<p> Thermal Coal   32,909 (ULD)  1,450     Nand Neeti	 24/11</p>
<p> Thermal Coal	130 (ULD) 36,694     Gem Of Madras    23/11</p>
<p> Iron Ore	  6,000 (LDD) 26,000     Jag Kanti	  28/11</p>
<p> Container	   115 (ULD)    311     Tiger Bridge     28/11</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>	    Note:</p>
<p>	    LDD - Loading</p>
<p>	    ULD - Unloading</p>
<p>(Source: J.M.Baxi &amp; Co, Madras)</p>
